{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And she called the name of YHWH.</b> Calling the name of YHWH is the prayer in which the praise of the Holy One, blessed be He, is expressed — whether in the thought of the one who prays or in his words. As they said, of blessed memory: 'A person should always arrange the praise of the Place and afterward pray.' For through this the one who prays directs his intention toward Elohim, blessed be He, in the manner of שִׁוִּיתִי ה' לְנֶגְדִּי תָמִיד (Psalms 16:8), and likewise קָרָאתִי שִׁמְךָ ה' (Lamentations 3:55), and likewise וּשְׁמוּאֵל בְּקֹרְאֵי שְׁמוֹ (Psalms 99:6), and likewise כִּי שֵׁם ה' אֶקְרָא (Deuteronomy 32:3). She said, then, that when she prayed she arranged the praise of Elohim, blessed be He, who had spoken to her, in saying <b>You are El Ro'i.</b> You are a God of seeing in every place — not in Abraham's house alone — as they said, of blessed memory: 'All the gates were locked except the gates of injustice' (Bava Metzia 59a)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:24.307101655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}